From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:06:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: draw layers

PushLayer and PopLayer were stubs, and the ID2D1DeviceContext PushLayer did
not even count as a push, so the PopLayer after it was an unbalanced pop, an
error that stopped all drawing up to EndDraw; command lists play their layers
back through it.

A layer pushed on a bitmap target now gets a bitmap of the target's size and
format, cleared, or a copy of the target when it is to start from what is
there, and what is drawn goes to it while the target the application set stays
the target; the content bounds clip it.  PopLayer puts it back through the
geometric mask, in the space the layer was pushed in as the mask transform takes
it, or through the content bounds without one, at the layer's opacity and
through its opacity brush, one pixel of the layer for each of the target's.
Layers left pushed are let go of at EndDraw, a new target and the end of the
context.  Ignoring alpha is not done.

The tests check opacity, layers in layers, content bounds, geometric masks and
their transform, the layers of ID2D1DeviceContext and a layer left pushed, as
they follow from the documentation; they were not run on Windows.  d2d1: 17925
tests, 0 failures, on Vulkan and in four of five runs on GL; one GL run ended
early without its summary, which did not happen again with exceptions logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 134a1665a538df9b933dd60e005284a7b341a4fe)

